.TH WELLDOCTOR 1 "2026" "wellutils 1.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
welldoctor \- system health check
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B welldoctor
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs read-only checks and prints one status line per check plus a summary:
S.M.A.R.T. health of fixed disks, CPU temperature thresholds, root
filesystem usage, failed systemd units, leftover .pacnew/.pacsave files and
orphan packages.
.PP
Designed for cron/systemd timers: the exit code reflects the worst finding.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All checks passed.
.TP
.B 1
Warnings found.
.TP
.B 2
Critical findings (failing S.M.A.R.T., temperature >= 85C, root fs >= 90%).
.TP
.B 3
Runtime error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
welldoctor && echo OK || echo "check your mail"
welldoctor --json | jq .summary
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smartctl (8),
.BR pacdiff (8),
.BR wellutils (1)
